@node Dataflow
@chapter Dataflow

@cindex dataflow
@cindex patterns
A mode's @code{pattern} chooses how it is laid out on the 4x4 mesh.  The single
register per PE and edge-only operand injection (north per column, west per row)
are the constraints every pattern works within.

@table @code
@item diagonal
@cindex diagonal pattern
Element-wise binary ops.  @var{a} enters from the north edge, @var{b} from the
west; PEs above the diagonal @code{pass} @var{a} southward, those below
@code{pass} @var{b} eastward, and each diagonal PE computes one result.  Four
lanes per transaction; @code{out = diag}.

@item reduce
@cindex reduce pattern
Accumulation into PE(0,0) with @code{mac}/@code{acc}: one element pair per step,
folded into the register, giving a scalar (e.g.@: @code{dot}).

@item custom
@cindex custom pattern
You place each PE with @code{pe R,C = @dots{}}; unlisted PEs are @code{nop}.
Output taps default to the diagonal, or a single @code{pe R,C} via @code{out}.

@item systolic
@cindex systolic pattern
@cindex weight-stationary
Weight-stationary matrix--vector @code{y = A*x}, driven by @command{cgra
matvec}.  The vector @var{x} is held stationary in the PE immediates; the
matrix streams in one row per step as a wavefront marching south (row 0
multiplies, rows 1--3 form a delay line).  The array is tiled over 4x4 blocks
for any @code{M x N}; the host sums the four skewed partials per output.

@item conv
@cindex convolution
1-D convolution as a Toeplitz matrix--vector (@command{cgra conv}).

@item scan
@cindex prefix scan
Inclusive prefix scan on row 0 (@command{cgra scan}): the element sits in the
immediate and is re-added each step while the running prefix flows west to
east, tiled over columns with the carry chained between blocks.
@end table

@cindex why weight-stationary
@section Why weight-stationary, not a full TPU array
A classical output-stationary systolic array fuses, in each PE, a multiply with
the accumulation of a partial sum arriving from a neighbour, while activations
flow orthogonally---two independent live values per PE.  This fabric gives each
PE a single register and admits external data only at two edges, so that fusion
is not realisable; the weight-stationary streaming dataflow above is the
natural fit.  The consequence is visible in @command{cgra bench}: cost is set by
serial round trips, not by the array.
